1 0 0 1 54 297.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/app.py is the orchestration layer. It exposes the FastAPI routes, initializes the database on startup, stores uploads, combines OCR, retrieval, external verification, report generation, resume insights, and persistence, and exposes the review and dashboard endpoints.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 284.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/ocr.py handles extraction and analysis. It supports text, image, and PDF input, extracts fields, builds verification output, flags fraud signals, calculates risk, and creates the template background report.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 271.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/rag.py provides local retrieval. It loads corpus text, builds an in-memory embedding index, and returns similar documents for the current upload.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 258.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/connectors.py implements the external verification skeleton. It includes mock employment and identity checks, live request retry logic, and normalized connector results.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 245.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/llm_report.py manages optional LLM report generation. It builds the Ollama prompt, calls the local Ollama HTTP endpoint, and falls back to the template report when the LLM call fails.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 232.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/db.py owns storage and analytics. It creates the SQLite schema, saves cases, reads cases, lists pending reviews, applies review decisions, and computes dashboard summary metrics.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 219.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/insights.py parses resume text for dashboard charts. It extracts experience buckets, education buckets, and top skills from resume text.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 206.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/templates/upload.html is the demo analyzer page. It has the upload form, report-only form, and output sections for assessment, external verification, report text, and raw JSON.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 193.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(src/templates/dashboard.html is the HR dashboard page. It shows KPI cards, a review overview, recent cases, and charts for experience, education, and top skills.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 180.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(docs/DESIGN.md explains the intended logical architecture, the local-first model policy, and why Ollama and MiniLM are preferred.) Tj
1 0 0 1 54 167.89 Tm
/F1 11 Tf
(docs/MODEL_SELECTION_REPORT.md explains the model choice tradeoffs and why sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 is the preferred retrieval model.) Tj
